/-!
# The relative Maslov grading of generators

Let `(Σ, α, β, z)` be a pointed Heegaard diagram with `n` attaching curves of each kind and a
single basepoint `z`. The Heegaard Floer chain group `CF̂` is relatively graded: for generators
`x`, `y` joined by a domain `D`, the *relative Maslov grading* is

`gr(x, y) = μ(D) - 2 n_z(D)`,

where `μ` is the combinatorial Maslov index `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.maslovIndex` and
`n_z(D)` is the multiplicity of `D` at the basepoint. The hat differential counts holomorphic
disks of Maslov index one avoiding the basepoint, so it lowers `gr` by one.

Two domains from `x` to `y` differ by a domain from `x` to `x`. With a single basepoint, such a
domain is a periodic domain plus a multiple of the whole surface `Σ`, the domain `1`. The whole
surface has `n_z(Σ) = 1` and, when the Euler characteristics `χ` of the regions are those of the
regions of a closed surface of genus `n`, Maslov index `μ(Σ) = 2`. So it does not change `gr`,
while a periodic domain `P` changes it by `μ(P)`. Hence `gr` is well defined as soon as every
periodic domain has Maslov index zero at `x`. On a geometric diagram `μ(P)` is the evaluation of
the first Chern class of the spin^c structure of `x` on the homology class of `P`, so this holds
for the generators of a torsion spin^c structure, and in particular when `b₁(Y) = 0`, when the
only periodic domain is zero. Without it `gr` genuinely depends on the domain: for the
genus-one diagram of `S¹ × S²` with its basepoint in a bigon, the two bigons from `p₀` to `p₁`
give the values `-1` and `1`
(`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.maslovIndex_sub_two_mul_circleTimesSphere_one`).

In general `gr` is a relative grading modulo the Maslov indices of the periodic domains at `x`,
the subgroup `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.periodicMaslovIndices` of `ℚ`. On a geometric diagram,
by the evaluation of the first Chern class recalled above (not formalized here), this is the
image of the pairing of `c₁(s_z(x))` with `H₂(Y; ℤ)`, so it is `d(s) ℤ` for the divisibility
`d(s)` of `c₁(s_z(x))`, and `gr` is the relative `ℤ / d(s)` grading of Ozsváth and Szabó.
Combinatorially the subgroup is cyclic, generated by some `d ≥ 0`, because every Maslov index is
a multiple of `1 / 4`. It is the same at generators joined by a domain, and the
class of `μ(D) - 2 n_z(D)` in the quotient of `ℚ` by it does not depend on the domain `D` from
`x` to `y`. The value `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.relativeGrading` computed from a chosen domain
is therefore a representative of this class, additive and antisymmetric modulo the subgroup, and
the hat differential lowers it by one modulo the subgroup. The ℚ-valued statements above are the
case where the subgroup is zero.

The Euler characteristics are not determined by the incidence data, so they are an explicit
argument `χ`, normalized by `∑ χ(R) - #(α ∩ β) = 2 - 2n`. The left side is the Euler
characteristic of the surface assembled from the regions, the `2 #(α ∩ β)` arcs and the
intersection points, so this says that the surface has genus `n`, as for a pointed Heegaard
diagram.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.periodicMaslovIndices`: the subgroup of `ℚ` of Maslov indices of
  periodic domains at a generator.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.relativeGrading`: the relative grading `gr(x, y)`, computed from
  a chosen domain from `x` to `y`, or `0` when there is none.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.exists_nonneg_periodicMaslovIndices_eq_zmultiples`: the
  subgroup of periodic Maslov indices is generated by some `d ≥ 0`.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.IsDomainBetween.periodicMaslovIndices_eq`: it is the same at
  generators joined by a domain.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.IsDomainBetween.coe_relativeGrading_eq`: modulo the periodic
  Maslov indices, the relative grading is `μ(D) - 2 n_z(D)` for every domain `D` from `x` to `y`.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.IsDomainBetween.coe_relativeGrading_add` and
  `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.IsDomainBetween.coe_relativeGrading_swap`: additivity and
  antisymmetry modulo the periodic Maslov indices.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.IsDomainBetween.maslovIndex_self_eq_two_mul`: a domain from `x`
  to `x` has Maslov index `2 n_z`.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.IsDomainBetween.maslovIndex_sub_two_mul_eq`: `μ(D) - 2 n_z(D)` is
  the same for all domains `D` from `x` to `y`.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.IsDomainBetween.relativeGrading_eq`: the relative grading is
  `μ(D) - 2 n_z(D)` for every domain `D` from `x` to `y`.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.IsDomainBetween.relativeGrading_add`:
  `gr(x, y) + gr(y, w) = gr(x, w)`.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.IsDomainBetween.relativeGrading_swap`: `gr(y, x) = -gr(x, y)`.

## References

* P. Ozsváth and Z. Szabó, *Holomorphic disks and topological invariants for closed
  three-manifolds*, Ann. of Math. **159** (2004),
  [arXiv:math/0101206](https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0101206): the relative grading
  `gr(x, y) = μ(φ) - 2 n_z(φ)`, the class of the whole surface with Maslov index two and basepoint
  multiplicity one, and the evaluation of the first Chern class as the Maslov index of a periodic
  domain.
* R. Lipshitz, *A cylindrical reformulation of Heegaard Floer homology*, Geom. Topol. **10**
  (2006), [arXiv:math/0502404](https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0502404), §4, for the index formula
  `μ(D) = e(D) + n_x(D) + n_y(D)`.
-/

public section

namespace TauCeti

namespace HeegaardRegionSystem

universe u v w

variable {n : ℕ} {Point : Type u} {Region : Type v} {Basepoint : Type w}
  {H : HeegaardRegionSystem n Point Region Basepoint}

variable [Fintype Point] [DecidableEq Region] [Fintype Region]

section PeriodicMaslovIndices

variable {χ : Region → ℤ} {x y : H.Generator} {D P : Region → ℤ}

variable (H) in
/-- The Maslov indices at the generator `x` of the periodic domains, a subgroup of `ℚ`. In a
singly pointed diagram the relative grading is well defined modulo this subgroup
(`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.IsDomainBetween.coe_relativeGrading_eq`). On a geometric diagram,
by Ozsváth and Szabó (not formalized here), it is the image of the pairing of `c₁(s_z(x))` with
`H₂(Y; ℤ)`. -/
def periodicMaslovIndices (χ : Region → ℤ) (x : H.Generator) : AddSubgroup ℚ :=
  H.periodicDomains.map (H.maslovIndex χ x x)

/-- The periodic Maslov indices are the image of the periodic domains under the Maslov index. -/
theorem periodicMaslovIndices_def :
    H.periodicMaslovIndices χ x = H.periodicDomains.map (H.maslovIndex χ x x) :=
  (rfl)

/-- A rational number is a periodic Maslov index at `x` when it is the Maslov index at `x` of a
periodic domain. -/
@[simp]
theorem mem_periodicMaslovIndices_iff {q : ℚ} :
    q ∈ H.periodicMaslovIndices χ x ↔ ∃ P ∈ H.periodicDomains, H.maslovIndex χ x x P = q :=
  AddSubgroup.mem_map

/-- The Maslov index at `x` of a periodic domain is a periodic Maslov index at `x`. -/
theorem maslovIndex_mem_periodicMaslovIndices (hP : P ∈ H.periodicDomains) :
    H.maslovIndex χ x x P ∈ H.periodicMaslovIndices χ x :=
  AddSubgroup.mem_map_of_mem _ hP

/-- The periodic Maslov indices at `x` vanish exactly when every periodic domain has Maslov
index zero at `x`, the hypothesis of the `ℚ`-valued relative grading. -/
theorem periodicMaslovIndices_eq_bot_iff :
    H.periodicMaslovIndices χ x = ⊥ ↔ ∀ P ∈ H.periodicDomains, H.maslovIndex χ x x P = 0 :=
  (AddSubgroup.map_eq_bot_iff _).trans ⟨fun h _ hP => h hP, fun h P hP => h P hP⟩

/-- Generators joined by a domain have the same periodic Maslov indices. -/
theorem IsDomainBetween.periodicMaslovIndices_eq (hD : H.IsDomainBetween x y D) :
    H.periodicMaslovIndices χ x = H.periodicMaslovIndices χ y := by
  ext q
  simp only [mem_periodicMaslovIndices_iff]
  refine exists_congr fun P => and_congr_right fun hP => ?_
  rw [hD.maslovIndex_self_eq χ (isDomainBetween_self_iff.mpr hP).1]

variable (H) in
/-- The periodic Maslov indices at `x` are the integer multiples of some `d ≥ 0`, the
combinatorial counterpart of the divisibility `d(s)` of `c₁(s)`. The subgroup is cyclic because
every Maslov index is an integer multiple of `1 / 4`. -/
theorem exists_nonneg_periodicMaslovIndices_eq_zmultiples (χ : Region → ℤ) (x : H.Generator) :
    ∃ d : ℚ, 0 ≤ d ∧ H.periodicMaslovIndices χ x = AddSubgroup.zmultiples d := by
  have hle : H.periodicMaslovIndices χ x ≤ AddSubgroup.zmultiples (4⁻¹ : ℚ) := fun q hq => by
    obtain ⟨P, -, rfl⟩ := mem_periodicMaslovIndices_iff.mp hq
    exact H.maslovIndex_mem_zmultiples_inv_four χ x x P
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := (AddSubgroup.le_zmultiples_iff _ _).mp hle
  exact ⟨k • 4⁻¹, by positivity, hk⟩

end PeriodicMaslovIndices

open scoped Classical in
variable (H) in
/-- The relative Maslov grading `gr(x, y) = μ(D) - 2 n_z(D)` of two generators, for a chosen
domain `D` from `x` to `y`, or `0` when no domain joins them. In a singly pointed diagram
satisfying the Euler normalization, its class modulo the periodic Maslov indices at `x` does not
depend on the choice of `D` (`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.IsDomainBetween.coe_relativeGrading_eq`),
and when the periodic domains have Maslov index zero at the source generator neither does the
value itself (`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.IsDomainBetween.relativeGrading_eq`). -/
noncomputable def relativeGrading (χ : Region → ℤ) (z : Basepoint) (x y : H.Generator) : ℚ :=
  if h : ∃ D, H.IsDomainBetween x y D then
    H.maslovIndex χ x y h.choose - 2 * h.choose (H.basepoint z)
  else 0

variable [Subsingleton Basepoint] {χ : Region → ℤ} (z : Basepoint)
  (hχ : ∑ r, χ r - Fintype.card Point = 2 - 2 * (n : ℤ)) {x y w : H.Generator}
  {D D' E : Region → ℤ}

include hχ

/-- In a singly pointed diagram of a closed surface of genus `n`, a domain `E` from `x` to `x`
has `μ(E) - 2 n_z(E)` among the periodic Maslov indices at `x`: it is a periodic domain plus
`n_z(E)` copies of the whole surface, which has Maslov index two. -/
theorem IsDomainBetween.maslovIndex_sub_two_mul_mem_periodicMaslovIndices
    (hE : H.IsDomainBetween x x E) :
    H.maslovIndex χ x x E - 2 * E (H.basepoint z) ∈ H.periodicMaslovIndices χ x := by
  have h := maslovIndex_mem_periodicMaslovIndices (χ := χ) (x := x)
    ((isDomainBetween_self_iff_sub_smul_one_mem_periodicDomains z).mp hE)
  rwa [map_sub, map_zsmul, maslovIndex_one_eq_two hχ, zsmul_eq_mul, mul_comm] at h

/-- In a singly pointed diagram of a closed surface of genus `n` all of whose periodic domains
have Maslov index zero at `x`, a domain `E` from `x` to `x` has Maslov index `2 n_z(E)`: it is a
periodic domain plus `n_z(E)` copies of the whole surface. -/
theorem IsDomainBetween.maslovIndex_self_eq_two_mul
    (hP : ∀ P ∈ H.periodicDomains, H.maslovIndex χ x x P = 0) (hE : H.IsDomainBetween x x E) :
    H.maslovIndex χ x x E = 2 * E (H.basepoint z) := by
  have h := hE.maslovIndex_sub_two_mul_mem_periodicMaslovIndices z hχ
  rwa [periodicMaslovIndices_eq_bot_iff.mpr hP, AddSubgroup.mem_bot, sub_eq_zero] at h

/-- In a singly pointed diagram of a closed surface of genus `n`, the quantities
`μ(D) - 2 n_z(D)` for domains `D` from `x` to `y` differ by periodic Maslov indices at `x`. -/
theorem IsDomainBetween.maslovIndex_sub_two_mul_sub_mem_periodicMaslovIndices
    (hD : H.IsDomainBetween x y D) (hD' : H.IsDomainBetween x y D') :
    H.maslovIndex χ x y D - 2 * D (H.basepoint z) -
        (H.maslovIndex χ x y D' - 2 * D' (H.basepoint z)) ∈ H.periodicMaslovIndices χ x := by
  -- `D - D'` runs from `x` to `x`, and both sides of its index count split along `y`.
  have h := (hD.add hD'.neg).maslovIndex_sub_two_mul_mem_periodicMaslovIndices z hχ
  rw [hD.maslovIndex_add χ hD'.neg, maslovIndex_neg] at h
  convert h using 1
  push_cast [Pi.add_apply, Pi.neg_apply]
  ring

/-- In a singly pointed diagram of a closed surface of genus `n` all of whose periodic domains
have Maslov index zero at `x`, the quantity `μ(D) - 2 n_z(D)` is the same for all domains `D`
from `x` to `y`. -/
theorem IsDomainBetween.maslovIndex_sub_two_mul_eq
    (hP : ∀ P ∈ H.periodicDomains, H.maslovIndex χ x x P = 0) (hD : H.IsDomainBetween x y D)
    (hD' : H.IsDomainBetween x y D') :
    H.maslovIndex χ x y D - 2 * D (H.basepoint z) =
      H.maslovIndex χ x y D' - 2 * D' (H.basepoint z) := by
  have h := hD.maslovIndex_sub_two_mul_sub_mem_periodicMaslovIndices z hχ hD'
  rwa [periodicMaslovIndices_eq_bot_iff.mpr hP, AddSubgroup.mem_bot, sub_eq_zero] at h

omit hχ [Subsingleton Basepoint] in
/-- When no domain joins `x` to `y`, the relative grading is `0`. -/
theorem relativeGrading_of_forall_not_isDomainBetween
    (h : ∀ D, ¬H.IsDomainBetween x y D) : H.relativeGrading χ z x y = 0 := by
  rw [relativeGrading, dite_eq_right (not_exists.mpr h)]

/-- Modulo the periodic Maslov indices at `x`, the relative grading is `μ(D) - 2 n_z(D)` for
every domain `D` from `x` to `y`. This is the combinatorial counterpart of the relative
`ℤ / d(s)` grading of Ozsváth and Szabó; the identification with `c₁` is not formalized here. -/
theorem IsDomainBetween.coe_relativeGrading_eq (hD : H.IsDomainBetween x y D) :
    (H.relativeGrading χ z x y : ℚ ⧸ H.periodicMaslovIndices χ x) =
      ((H.maslovIndex χ x y D - 2 * D (H.basepoint z) : ℚ) : ℚ ⧸ H.periodicMaslovIndices χ x) := by
  have h : ∃ D, H.IsDomainBetween x y D := ⟨D, hD⟩
  rw [QuotientAddGroup.eq_iff_sub_mem, relativeGrading, dite_eq_left h]
  exact h.choose_spec.maslovIndex_sub_two_mul_sub_mem_periodicMaslovIndices z hχ hD

/-- The relative grading is `μ(D) - 2 n_z(D)` for every domain `D` from `x` to `y`, when the
periodic domains have Maslov index zero at `x`. -/
theorem IsDomainBetween.relativeGrading_eq
    (hP : ∀ P ∈ H.periodicDomains, H.maslovIndex χ x x P = 0) (hD : H.IsDomainBetween x y D) :
    H.relativeGrading χ z x y = H.maslovIndex χ x y D - 2 * D (H.basepoint z) := by
  have h := QuotientAddGroup.eq_iff_sub_mem.mp (hD.coe_relativeGrading_eq z hχ)
  rwa [periodicMaslovIndices_eq_bot_iff.mpr hP, AddSubgroup.mem_bot, sub_eq_zero] at h

/-- A generator has relative grading zero with itself, modulo the periodic Maslov indices. -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_relativeGrading_self :
    (H.relativeGrading χ z x x : ℚ ⧸ H.periodicMaslovIndices χ x) = 0 := by
  simp [(isDomainBetween_zero x).coe_relativeGrading_eq z hχ]

/-- The relative grading is additive modulo the periodic Maslov indices:
`gr(x, y) + gr(y, w) = gr(x, w)` for generators joined by domains. -/
theorem IsDomainBetween.coe_relativeGrading_add (hD : H.IsDomainBetween x y D)
    (hE : H.IsDomainBetween y w E) :
    ((H.relativeGrading χ z x y + H.relativeGrading χ z y w : ℚ) :
        ℚ ⧸ H.periodicMaslovIndices χ x) = H.relativeGrading χ z x w := by
  have hxy := QuotientAddGroup.eq_iff_sub_mem.mp (hD.coe_relativeGrading_eq z hχ)
  have hyw := QuotientAddGroup.eq_iff_sub_mem.mp (hE.coe_relativeGrading_eq z hχ)
  have hxw := QuotientAddGroup.eq_iff_sub_mem.mp ((hD.add hE).coe_relativeGrading_eq z hχ)
  rw [← hD.periodicMaslovIndices_eq] at hyw
  rw [QuotientAddGroup.eq_iff_sub_mem]
  convert sub_mem (add_mem hxy hyw) hxw using 1
  rw [hD.maslovIndex_add χ hE, Pi.add_apply, Int.cast_add]
  ring

/-- The relative grading is antisymmetric modulo the periodic Maslov indices:
`gr(y, x) = -gr(x, y)` for generators joined by a domain. -/
theorem IsDomainBetween.coe_relativeGrading_swap (hD : H.IsDomainBetween x y D) :
    (H.relativeGrading χ z y x : ℚ ⧸ H.periodicMaslovIndices χ x) =
      -(H.relativeGrading χ z x y : ℚ ⧸ H.periodicMaslovIndices χ x) := by
  have hxy := QuotientAddGroup.eq_iff_sub_mem.mp (hD.coe_relativeGrading_eq z hχ)
  have hyx := QuotientAddGroup.eq_iff_sub_mem.mp (hD.neg.coe_relativeGrading_eq z hχ)
  rw [← hD.periodicMaslovIndices_eq] at hyx
  rw [← QuotientAddGroup.mk_neg, QuotientAddGroup.eq_iff_sub_mem]
  convert add_mem hyx hxy using 1
  rw [maslovIndex_neg, Pi.neg_apply, Int.cast_neg]
  ring

/-- A generator has relative grading zero with itself. -/
@[simp]
theorem relativeGrading_self (hP : ∀ P ∈ H.periodicDomains, H.maslovIndex χ x x P = 0) :
    H.relativeGrading χ z x x = 0 := by
  simp [(isDomainBetween_zero x).relativeGrading_eq z hχ hP]

/-- The relative grading is additive: `gr(x, y) + gr(y, w) = gr(x, w)` for generators joined by
domains, when the periodic domains have Maslov index zero at `x`. -/
theorem IsDomainBetween.relativeGrading_add
    (hP : ∀ P ∈ H.periodicDomains, H.maslovIndex χ x x P = 0) (hD : H.IsDomainBetween x y D)
    (hE : H.IsDomainBetween y w E) :
    H.relativeGrading χ z x y + H.relativeGrading χ z y w = H.relativeGrading χ z x w := by
  rw [hD.relativeGrading_eq z hχ hP,
    hE.relativeGrading_eq z hχ (hD.forall_mem_periodicDomains_maslovIndex_eq_zero χ hP),
    (hD.add hE).relativeGrading_eq z hχ hP, hD.maslovIndex_add χ hE, Pi.add_apply, Int.cast_add]
  ring

/-- The relative grading is antisymmetric: `gr(y, x) = -gr(x, y)` for generators joined by a
domain, when the periodic domains have Maslov index zero at `x`. -/
theorem IsDomainBetween.relativeGrading_swap
    (hP : ∀ P ∈ H.periodicDomains, H.maslovIndex χ x x P = 0) (hD : H.IsDomainBetween x y D) :
    H.relativeGrading χ z y x = -H.relativeGrading χ z x y := by
  rw [hD.relativeGrading_eq z hχ hP,
    hD.neg.relativeGrading_eq z hχ (hD.forall_mem_periodicDomains_maslovIndex_eq_zero χ hP),
    maslovIndex_neg, Pi.neg_apply, Int.cast_neg]
  ring

end HeegaardRegionSystem

end TauCeti
